-- title:
--   Round-six certificates of the integer-multiplication κ-record (κ = 3666565558019/10¹⁷)
-- statement:
--   The five computational certificates of round six of the integer-multiplication κ-record (Jain, repository `integer-mult-kappa`, file `lean/Round6.lean`), checked exactly as published:
--
--   1. **Bit-phase rank sum.** For the bit-interchange histogram — width classes $(w, n)$ with $w \in \{1,3,\dots,23\}$ plus two tail classes $(439, 6\,272\,882)$ and $(483, 141\,952\,734)$ — the weighted rank sum $\sum w\,n$ equals $78\,410\,006\,675$.
--
--   2. **Bit-phase moment bound.** With savings $a = 36\,667/10^9$, base width $m = 529$ and work budget $W = 148\,225\,616$: every width satisfies $w < m$ and $a \cdot L_w < 1$ where $L_w = \operatorname{lnUp}(m/w)$, and $\sum n\,w / (m\,(1 - a L_w)) < W$.
--
--   3. **Complex-phase rank sum.** For the complex-interchange histogram (width classes $1$ to $24$ plus tail classes $(529, 8\,193\,152)$ and $(552, 199\,193\,984)$), $\sum w\,n = 119\,453\,132\,304$.
--
--   4. **Complex-phase moment bound.** With $a = 36\,926\,111 / (5\cdot 10^{11})$, $m = 576$, $W = 207\,387\,136$: every width $w < m$, $a L_w < 1$, and $\sum n w / (m(1 - a L_w)) < W$.
--
--   5. **Parameter assembly.** With the two savings above, split $\beta = 1/1000$, tolerances $\varepsilon = 2\,499\,908\,335\,861\,049 / (25\cdot 10^{14})$ and $x = 14\,695$, constant $c_1 = 14\,694$, and $m_c = 576$, $s_c = 119\,453\,132\,304$: the assembly guard `kappaOK` holds — $c_1 \ge 2 + m_c \ln s_c$, all strict consistency constraints are satisfied, and every cost margin exceeds $\kappa = 3\,666\,565\,558\,019/10^{17} \approx 3.67\cdot 10^{-5}$.
--
--   Together these are the complete finite-certificate content of round six: the strongest published κ-savings claim for integer multiplication, the value targeted by [`IntMul.Kappa.jain_round6`](p2m:theorem/9963d73f-fab7-44ad-b490-192b4d9f47b1). Every claim here is a finite computation over explicit rational data, discharged by `decide` in the Lean kernel.
-- source:
--   Swapnil Jain, integer-mult-kappa, https://github.com/Swapnil-jain/integer-mult-kappa, file lean/Round6.lean — the five round-six certificates (generated by lean/gen.py from round6-histograms.json); target of the mission 'Integer Multiplication in O(n (log n)^(1-κ)) Time'.

